@*
    What a commit moves on in the Repair Spec section, carried forward by the
    script after every commit: the identity of each line as the Case now
    holds it, by the row it was posted from, and the spec the commit wrote.
    Every save writes its lines afresh, so the rows the operator keeps typing
    in take the ids the save gave them, and the next commit names lines the
    Case still has. A new spec's first commit creates it, so the editor and
    the page address take its id, and the next commit edits that spec rather
    than creating another. Both are disabled, so they post nothing.
*@
@model Pegasus.Web.Pages.Cases.DetailsModel
<input type="hidden" name="estimateLineIds" value="@Model.EstimateLineIdentities" form="case-edit-form" disabled data-carry-forward data-estimate-line-ids />
<input type="hidden" name="estimateWritten" value="@Model.WrittenEstimateId" form="case-edit-form" disabled data-carry-forward data-estimate-written />
